just get you one from the mall.

00:01:35.622 --> 00:01:37.277
(Jing and Tway laugh)

00:01:37.277 --> 00:01:40.260
- That's a decent constellation
prize, but I believe in you.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.093
- Thank you.

00:01:41.093 --> 00:01:42.150
- So, I will see you soon.

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:43.260
- I'll see you later.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:44.410
- All right. Good luck.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:48.060
- Wow. Okay.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.114
Let's make a big, giant cinnamon roll.

00:01:52.114 --> 00:01:54.781
(holiday music)

00:01:57.390 --> 00:02:00.450
- I'm gonna start off by making the dough.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.590
So I have all purpose flour here

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.870
and I'm also using whole wheat flour.

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:08.340
This is going to help

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.280
with the structure of the cinnamon roll.

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:12.933
I have my sugar here.

00:02:13.770 --> 00:02:18.420
Oh, and by the way, this is
only one batch of the dough.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:23.280
Some salt, ginger, and yeast.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.113
This dry mix.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:30.120
So this is 16 whole eggs.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:32.373
There's actually 32 in the recipe.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:37.740
A lot of butter in this recipe.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.240
And hey, I'm not mad at it.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.350
I love butter.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.450
I just feel like everything
in life that's good,

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.183
is bad for you and that's just not fair.

00:02:48.391 --> 00:02:50.253
I have my milk over here.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.793
Molasses.

00:02:55.616 --> 00:02:57.260
Oh, yeah.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:59.040
So this is a holiday recipe,

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.110
and that's why we're using molasses

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.413
to give it that, you know,
extra holiday flavor.

00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:09.963
All right, and I think it's
time to add the dry in.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:14.730
Working with this much
dough kind of scares me,

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.700
because I just hope that it rises.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.200
For next season, can production get like

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.987
a commercial mixer or what?

00:03:25.987 --> 00:03:28.953
Are we just gonna continue
to do this by hand?

00:03:30.983 --> 00:03:32.130
Ooh.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:36.813
Think I'm ready to put
this out onto the counter.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:39.683
Here we go.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:45.810
So my dough is getting
there, but in the meantime

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:48.630
Tiny Tway is here to
entertain us with some facts.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:49.923
So let's hear it.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:53.790
So it was the Egyptians and the Romans

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:56.430
that had the original sticky bun,

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.350
but it was actually the Swedish

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:01.050
and the German immigrants
that brought their version

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.330
of the sticky buns to America.

00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:08.010
And it wasn't until the
1950s where the cinnamon role

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:11.130
as we know it, the ones
that I'm making now

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:14.313
was created and gained popularity.

00:04:15.810 --> 00:04:20.810
I think we are ready to go in the bowls.

00:04:22.154 --> 00:04:25.404
(upbeat ticking music)

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:29.250
So while the dough is rising

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.290
I'm going to make the filling,

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:34.230
